Given equation of parabola is
$y^2-k x+8=0\begin{array}{lr}\Rightarrow & y^2=k\left(x-\frac{8}{k}\right) \\ \Rightarrow & (y-0)^2=k\left(x-\frac{8}{k}\right)\end{array}
The equation of the directrix of this parabola is
$ x-$\frac{8}{k}=-\frac{k}{4} \quad[\because$ x=-a]\Rightarrow \quad x=$\frac{8}{k}-\frac{k}{4}
But the equation of the directrix is given as $ x-1=0$.
$\therefore \quad $\frac{8}{k}-\frac{k}{4}= 1\begin{aligned} \Rightarrow$& & k²+4 k-32 & =0 \\ \Rightarrow & & (k-4)(k+8) & =0 \\ \therefore & & k & =-8,4\end{aligned}

We have, $y^2+4 y+4 x+2=0\begin{aligned}
\Rightarrow & (y+2)^2+4 x-2 & =0 \\
\Rightarrow & (y+2)^2 & =-4\left(x-\frac{1}{2}\right)
\end{aligned}$
Replace, $\quad y+2=Y, x-\frac{1}{2}=X$
We have, $\quad Y^2=-4 X$
This is a parabola with directrix at $X=1$\begin{array}{lr}
\Rightarrow & x-$\frac{1}{2}=$1 \\
\Rightarrow & x=$\frac{3}{2}$
\end{array}
